// Logs — the structured agent-log push contract (W6-1). The agent tails its
// own structured (JSON-lines) log events and ships them two ways:
//   1. to Loki over the HTTP push API (queryable in the log stack), and
//   2. here, as LogBatch frames on the existing Stream uplink, where the
//      server keeps the indexed events in the log_events Timescale
//      hypertable so the RMM can surface recent events per device.
//
// Delivery is at-least-once: every entry carries a stable agent-generated
// id (content-derived), so the server dedups by id (ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING)
// and a re-sent batch after a reconnect is a no-op — same replay story as
// MetricBatch (idempotent on replay).

